  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Term Count Tests\n\nVerify that EffectiveBracket generates the correct number of terms.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Test 12: n=2 term count\n\nn=2 has only partition {2}, giving 1 term: BracketProjected[SF1, SF2, wH, wA]",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Create mock string fields for testing - use SF wrapper which SFTest recognizes *)\nSF1 = SF[R[c[0, z1], ct[0, z1bar]]];\nSF2 = SF[R[c[0, z2], ct[0, z2bar]]];\n\n(* First check if SFTest works *)\nPrint[\"SFTest[SF1]: \", SFTest[SF1]];\n\n(* Count terms by counting how many BracketProjected appear in the expanded result *)\ntest12 = EffectiveBracket[SF1, SF2];\nPrint[\"Result: \", test12];\n(* For n=2, there's exactly 1 partition {2} with 1 assignment, so 1 term *)\ntest12TermCount = Length[If[Head[test12] === Plus, List @@ test12, {test12}]];\ntest12Result = test12TermCount == 1;\nPrint[\"Test 12 (n=2 term count): \", test12TermCount, \" terms - \", If[test12Result, \"PASSED\", \"FAILED\"]];\ntest12Result",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
